WT vs Documented Mutant HEXA Protein Sequence Comparison
==========================================================

Gene: HEXA
Reference transcript: NM_000520.6
Reference protein: NP_000511.2

Documented variant:
NM_000520.6:c.1274_1277dup
Protein consequence: p.Tyr427fs
Mutation type: Frameshift

WT protein length: 529 amino acids
Mutant protein length: 431 amino acids

Nucleotide sequence around the mutation:
WT: TATC
Mutant:  TATCTATC-duplicated

Comparison:
The documented mutation duplicates four nucleotides, TATC, at
c.1274–c.1277. This four-nucleotide duplication causes a frameshift
beginning at approximately amino acid 427. The downstream amino-acid
sequence is changed and a premature stop codon is produced.

Conclusion:
The c.1274_1277dup mutation causes a frameshift and produces a
shorter predicted HEXA protein compared with the WT protein.
